claims:
{"zh": "Shég’ Xdaltth’í’（遗址号FAI-02043，旧称McDonald Creek）保存三个晚更新世文化层，年代约为13.8、13.0和12.7 ka。最早的C1层包含超过8万件考古材料；研究团队对其中大量遗物进行了三维定位，并识别出炉址、小型土坑、土炉、动物骨骼集中区以及可能的人工遮蔽/居住结构。遗物包括石器、骨针和其他骨器，以及野牛、猛犸象、马、兔、狼和多种鸟类等动物遗存。

66个AMS年代为遗址建立了坚实年代框架。最早文化层中一组带柄、菱形双面器在阿拉斯加中部十分罕见，却与白令陆桥西侧Nikita Lake和Berelekh的同期材料具有明显相似性。研究者因此把这一遗址视为连接白令陆桥东西两侧物质文化的重要证据。", "en": "Shég’ Xdaltth’í’ (FAI-02043, formerly McDonald Creek) preserves three Late Pleistocene archaeological components dating to about 13.8, 13.0 and 12.7 ka. The earliest component contains more than 80,000 archaeological specimens and unusually well-preserved spatial patterning, including hearths, a small pit, an earth oven, faunal concentrations and a probable artificial shelter or dwelling area. The assemblage includes lithics, bone needles and other osseous tools together with bison, mammoth, horse, hare, wolf and diverse bird remains.

Sixty-six AMS radiocarbon dates provide a robust chronology. A distinctive set of stemmed, diamond-shaped bifaces in the earliest component is unusual in central Alaska but resembles coeval artifacts at Nikita Lake and Berelekh in western Beringia. The authors therefore identify the site as an important archaeological link across the former Bering Land Bridge."}

{"zh": "10号墓的调查始于2025年：一则匿名举报提醒Centro INAH Oaxaca注意可能的盗掘活动，随后Jorge Bautista Hernández和Gabriela Galicia Moreno开展调查并定位墓室。INAH于2026年1月23日正式公布这一发现。墓位于Cerro de la Cantera，年代约公元600年，后续官方材料将其置于约公元600–900年的晚期古典时代。墓室保存阶梯式石板券顶、灰泥和彩绘装饰。入口处以猫头鹰形象构成大型雕塑元素，鸟喙覆盖或包围一张灰泥塑成并上色的人脸；门楣和门框保存历法名号与人物形象。墓内壁画以赭、白、绿、红、蓝等颜色描绘一列携带copal香料的人物。

目前正在进行陶器、图像学、铭文学和人骨分析。官方报道说明，墓室内只保存少量人骨碎片，墓外发现不同时期的小型陶器；因此关于墓主人身份、使用次数和谱系关系的解释仍未完成。", "en": "Investigation of Tomb 10 began in 2025 after an anonymous report alerted Centro INAH Oaxaca to possible looting; archaeologists Jorge Bautista Hernández and Gabriela Galicia Moreno subsequently located the tomb. INAH formally announced the discovery on 23 January 2026. Located at Cerro de la Cantera, the tomb dates to around AD 600; later official reporting places it within the Late Classic period, approximately AD 600–900. The chamber preserves stepped stone roofing, stucco and painted decoration. A large owl motif frames the entrance, with a modeled and painted human face emerging from or covered by the beak. The lintel and jambs preserve calendrical names and human figures, while murals in ochre, white, green, red and blue depict a procession of figures carrying copal.

Ceramic, iconographic, epigraphic and physical-anthropological analyses are ongoing. Official reporting notes that only limited human skeletal fragments survive inside the chamber and that miniature vessels of different periods were found outside it. Interpretation of the tomb occupant, reuse history and dynastic relationships is therefore still incomplete."}

{"zh": "10号墓的调查始于2025年：一则匿名举报提醒Centro INAH Oaxaca注意可能的盗掘活动，随后Jorge Bautista Hernández和Gabriela Galicia Moreno开展调查并定位墓室。INAH于2026年1月23日正式公布这一发现。墓位于Cerro de la Cantera，年代约公元600年，后续官方材料将其置于约公元600–900年的晚期古典时代。墓室保存阶梯式石板券顶、灰泥和彩绘装饰。入口处以猫头鹰形象构成大型雕塑元素，鸟喙覆盖或包围一张灰泥塑成并上色的人脸；门楣和门框保存历法名号与人物形象。墓内壁画以赭、白、绿、红、蓝等颜色描绘一列携带copal香料的人物。

